    "freeze_rule":  "Every pair generated by coverage_requirements must execute through the real Manager process entry on a disposable Windows installation. Every compatibility-shadow bypass action must have executable entry coverage. Any new PrimaryModeCount action absent from manager-entry-policy.json is a release blocker. A scenario harness may not restore state through the same runtime path under test and must publish a result record even when setup or cleanup fails. BindInstance coverage must execute a changed-path rebind transaction and assert the new registry path is committed without Manager-driven Hub-byte movement or cloning. UpdateManager coverage must seed a newer valid disposable Manager package and assert the successor is installed, self-test succeeds, and the restarted -UpdateManager process reaches its post-install no-newer-package completion path."
